      "kind": "crux",
      "subject": "שנאו נפשׁ דוד",
      "rationale": "Ketiv שנאו ('they hated') vs qere שנאי ('my haters'); the qere reads 'whom my nefesh hates', the ketiv 'whom David's nefesh hates'."
    },
    {
      "kind": "substitution",
      "subject": "nefesh",
      "rationale": "נפשׁ is throat\/life-force, the seat of desire and feeling — 'David's nefesh hates' is more visceral than an English 'soul' or plain 'David hated'."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wordplay",
      "subject": "עור ופסח",
      "rationale": "The Jebusites' taunt words from v. 6 (the blind and the lame) return as a fixed saying — the verse itself names the birth of a proverb."
    }
  ],
